  "composer": {
    "accepted_prose": "Tomi blinked, processing his words. The offer was oddly specific—and oddly careful. She leaned against the arm of the couch, one eyebrow lifting as she considered it. \"Huh.\" She tapped her fingers on the cushion. \"One loop, just holding a stopwatch, no coaching, no deciding whether I should train.\" She repeated the terms back, testing them. It was a narrow thing, almost absurdly limited. But that was exactly what made it feel safe. \"I mean... yeah, actually, it could be useful.\" She shrugged, a half-smile flickering. \"I've been trying to beat my reaction time on the recovery sets without pushing into sloppy form. Having someone call the start and stop cleanly—without telling me how to run—that's kind of what I need.\" She held up a finger. \"But it's once, and I give the instructions. You just press the button. Got it?\" Her tone was light but firm—a boundary drawn in chalk, not stone. She let the silence settle afterward, watching him to see if he understood.",
